# Scratch that `git am` leaves behind when a series is interrupted, re-applied or
# amended. Harmless, machine-specific, and must never reach the repository or a
# release. Note this is the repo's own ignore file and is unrelated to
# patches/.gitignore.baseline, which is the verbatim FileZilla .gitignore that the
# patch series restores inside the build work tree.
patches/series-backup/
series-backup/

# Local scratch and build output. None of this belongs in the repository: the kit
# is source plus scripts, and everything else is reproducible from them.
out/
install/
work/
logs/
build/
deps/
dl/
src/
*.log

  # Archives produced by the build.
*.7z
*.zip
  
# The source drop box. Pre-downloaded upstream tarballs can be dropped here and
# the fetch scripts will prefer them over the network, but they are large,
# third-party and reproducible - they are an input, not source. Only the
# directory and its instructions are tracked; drop a file in and it is ignored.
# Patterns must not be indented: gitignore treats leading whitespace as part of
# the pattern, so an indented "tarballs/*" silently matches nothing.
tarballs/*
!tarballs/.gitkeep
!tarballs/README.md

  

# Editor and OS noise.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
